;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Stack), §4.4 row pop, §2.5, §8.1 item 5 (count cases), tranche 2 plan Y5, task P1 item 2
;; expect: accept
;; result: 639
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 56
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: pop
;; One pop of a Vec of 640 allocates the copy of the tail and the new header, 2 objects: the vector of 640 (built by the bulk
;; builder from a range) costs 54 objects, measured alone, so the run is 56 (measured, the interpreter's count; under fibc the
;; same). Before the prelude had vec-pop (task P1) the pop rebuilt the first n-1 elements with the bulk builder, 54 more, 108
;; in all, and a rebuild by conj would add about 1340. The bound is the count, so it fails if the pop goes back to a rebuild.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (range 640))))
    (count (pop v))))
